<!-- Teaching layer over exact approved source fb8354e. -->
<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The app kept its operation key through a long offline period. The server kept the business result, but may already have forgotten the replay record. Retrying with the same key now has a boundary to cross.</p>

<!-- @before First Principles :: guide -->
### A replay window is part of the contract

An idempotency key is not an eternal receipt. Stripe API v1 documents parameter comparison, captured responses after execution begins, and reuse after pruning. Choose a retention or reconciliation policy that covers supported retries; do not copy an example TTL as a universal mobile guarantee. [Stripe API v1 replay rules](https://docs.stripe.com/api/idempotent_requests).

<!-- @before Internal Mechanics :: animation -->
